{"step_index":176,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T18:41:39Z","thinking":"**Refining The Integration**\n\nI'm now integrating the ReduxProvider into `src/app/layout.tsx`. I see the existing structure and am planning how to best wrap the children within the provider. It seems straightforward, but I want to make sure the implementation aligns perfectly with the intended architecture.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import type { Metadata } from \"next\";\nimport { Geist, Geist_Mono } from \"next/font/google\";\nimport \"./globals.css\";\nimport { ReduxProvider } from \"@/redux/provider\";\n\nconst geistSans = Geist({\n  variable: \"--font-geist-sans\",\n  subsets: [\"latin\"],\n});\n\nconst geistMono = Geist_Mono({\n  variable: \"--font-geist-mono\",\n  subsets: [\"latin\"],\n});\n\nexport const metadata: Metadata = {\n  title: \"Summarist - Gain more knowledge in less time\",\n  description: \"Read or listen to the key takeaways from the world's best non-fiction books.\",\n};\n\nexport default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  return (\n    <html\n      lang=\"en\"\n      className={`${geistSans.variable} ${geistMono.variable} h-full antialiased`}\n    >\n      <body className=\"min-h-full flex flex-col bg-white text-gray-900\">\n        <ReduxProvider>{children}</ReduxProvider>\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  );\n}\n","Description":"Created layout.tsx with ReduxProvider wrapper in scratch.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\ambat\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\c7e5dbbf-c810-4443-81c8-ce6c4ef145fb\\scratch\\layout.tsx","toolAction":"Creating layout file in scratch directory","toolSummary":"Write to file"}}]}
