{"step_index":196,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T18:42:30Z","thinking":"**Considering Layout Strategies**\n\nI've successfully created the search bar! Now, I'm evaluating layout options. I'm considering structuring layouts for internal pages, using a global shell client component in `src/app/layout.tsx`, or creating a layout within a route group like `(dashboard)`. The NextJS App Router's capabilities are definitely a factor.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import Sidebar from \"@/components/Sidebar\";\nimport Searchbar from \"@/components/Searchbar\";\nimport AuthModal from \"@/components/AuthModal\";\n\nexport default function DashboardLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex min-h-screen bg-white w-full\">\n      <Sidebar />\n      <div className=\"flex-1 flex flex-col min-w-0\">\n        <header className=\"h-20 border-b border-gray-100 flex items-center px-6 md:px-10 justify-between shrink-0 sticky top-0 bg-white z-30\">\n          <Searchbar />\n        </header>\n        <main className=\"flex-1 p-6 md:p-10 max-w-[1070px] w-full mx-auto pb-24\">\n          {children}\n        </main>\n      </div>\n      <AuthModal />\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n","Description":"Created scratch layout.tsx for (dashboard) route group in scratch.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\ambat\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\c7e5dbbf-c810-4443-81c8-ce6c4ef145fb\\scratch\\dashboardLayout.tsx","toolAction":"Creating dashboard layout file in scratch directory","toolSummary":"Write to file"}}]}
